  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Assistance to Populations Affected by Flooding in N&#x2019;Djamena and the Lac Province, Chad</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2014, the crisis unfolding in Lac Province, Chad has been characterized by numerous challenging factors, such as insecurity, flooding, large-scale and continuous population movements (internally displaced persons (IDPs), returnees) as well as community clashes and socioeconomic-related tensions. While Chad habitually faces seasonal flooding due to severe rains, the flooding in 2022 has been the worst flooding since 1961. The project aims to improve humanitarian support for the most vulnerable IDPs, returnees and migrants in the Lac province through: 1) Strengthening availability of data on impact of flooding, 2) Improving living conditions of vulnerable displaced households in Lac Province through Shelter and Non-Food Item assistance, and 3) Improving mental health and psychosocial wellbeing through community-based mental health and psychosocial support interventions.</narrative>
  </description>
